 * A single-file catalogue of every carbon-relevant dataset + the carbon
 * calculation math, pulled out of "Charlie's Place KBA — Forest Carbon
 * Assessment v4.6" so it can be reused across projects.
 *
 * This file is a REFERENCE, not a pipeline. Sourcing it defines asset IDs,
 * loader functions, and unit-conversion helpers; it does NOT run the RF /
 * ensemble / sampling analysis (that stays in the assessment script). Nothing
 * heavy executes on paste — loaders build lazy ee objects only. Call
 * printReference() to dump the catalogue to the console, or run the DEMO block
 * at the bottom (default OFF) to visualise a few layers over an AOI.
 *
 * ACCESS LEGEND (checked per asset below):
 *   [PUBLIC] native GEE catalog / community (sat-io) — readable by anyone
 *   [PRIVATE] project asset — must be shared with the running account
 *
 * UNITS CONVENTION: forest/soil carbon densities are kg C / m² unless noted.
 *   1 kg C/m² = 10 Mg C/ha.  1 Mg/ha (biomass) → carbon via AGB_TO_C_KGM2.
 * ===================================================================== ****/


// ========================================================================
// SECTION 1 — CARBON UNIT CONVERSIONS  (the calculation core)
// ========================================================================
// All biomass products are harmonised to the SAME quantity as the Sothe (2022)
// forest-carbon map: TOTAL biomass carbon = aboveground + belowground.
//   C (kg/m²) = AGB(Mg/ha) × (1 + BGB_RATIO) × CARBON_FRACTION × MGHA_TO_KGM2
//             = AGB(Mg/ha) × AGB_TO_C_KGM2
var BGB_RATIO       = 0.22;   // belowground:aboveground biomass ratio (national approx.)
var CARBON_FRACTION = 0.50;   // IPCC dry-biomass carbon fraction
var MGHA_TO_KGM2    = 0.10;   // Mg/ha → kg/m²
var AGB_TO_C_KGM2   = (1 + BGB_RATIO) * CARBON_FRACTION * MGHA_TO_KGM2;   // = 0.061

// SCANFI constant σ for ensemble weighting = Guindon 2024 AGB RMSE, carbon-converted.
var SCANFI_RMSE_AGB_MGHA = 38.70;                                   // t/ha (Guindon 2024)
var SCANFI_SIGMA_FC      = SCANFI_RMSE_AGB_MGHA * AGB_TO_C_KGM2;    // ≈ 2.361 kg C/m²
//
// ⚠ DISCREPANCY CARRIED OVER FROM v4.6 — the source script's HEADER changelog
//   and its Step-7 comment both state SCANFI σ ≈ 1.935–1.940 kg/m². That is the
//   OLD v4.4 value (38.70 × 0.1 × 0.5, i.e. aboveground-only, no BGB uplift).
//   The v4.6 CODE actually computes 38.70 × 0.061 = 2.361 (AGB+BGB). This file
//   uses the code value (2.361). Confirm which you intend before quoting a σ.
//
// ⚠ HARMONISATION CAVEAT — Sothe FC natively includes dead-plant carbon and uses
//   forest-type-specific root ratios; the single national BGB_RATIO above is an
//   approximation, so GEDI-RF and SCANFI carbon are only *approximately*
//   comparable to Sothe FC. Fine for an ensemble prior; state it in any report.

// AGB (Mg/ha) → forest carbon (kg C/m², AGB+BGB). Input is an ee.Image.
function agbToForestCarbon(agb_mgha) {
  return ee.Image(agb_mgha).multiply(AGB_TO_C_KGM2);
}

// Convenience scalar reporting: kg C/m² → Mg C/ha
function kgm2_to_Mgha(x) { return ee.Number(x).multiply(10); }


